# Fblthp's "You may plot nonland cards from the top of your library" (CR 702.170a, 116.2k): a special action at sorcery timing
# (any time its controller has priority in their main phase with the stack empty), for the top card of the controller's own
# library, and for no land. Bot1 has Mox Ruby's {R} and Mox Sapphire's {U} all through: with an Ornithopter on the stack the
# Lightning Bolt on top is not offered; on Bot2's turn, with Bot2's Mox Ruby on the stack, it is not either (it is not Bot1's
# main phase); and Bot2, whose library also holds a Lightning Bolt on top and who has {R}, is never offered it (it is not "your
# library" of Fblthp's controller, and Bot2 has no such rule). On turn three the Bolt is drawn and the Forest under it is a land.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Fblthp, Lost on the Range
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Forest
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Island x6
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Fblthp, Lost on the Range.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
! Bot1.Library.Lightning Bolt.Activate(Ability: Plot)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
! Bot1.Library.Lightning Bolt.Activate(Ability: Plot)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot2.Library.Lightning Bolt.Activate(Ability: Plot)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Lightning Bolt
! Bot1.Library.Forest.Activate(Ability: Plot)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot2.Library.Count = 12
